				\begin{document}$$\bar{1}00$$\end{document}1¯00AL Bragg peaks, but corrected the last two values by +45° and −45°, respectively. We used the Williamson–Hall method49 to analyze the size of the WAXS Bragg peaks at each spatial point of the supercrystal. The FWHM of the Bragg peak is determined by the NC size and the lattice distortion as follows:1\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
